                {
                  "id": "lede",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Your trailers work hard every day, hauling valuable cargo across thousands of miles in changing road and weather conditions. Like any piece of commercial equipment, they experience wear over time. The difference between a reliable trailer and one sitting on the side of the road often comes down to one thing: consistent trailer service.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full",
                    "anchor": "post-lede"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-intro-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Waiting until something breaks almost always leads to more expensive repairs, unexpected downtime, and missed deliveries. Regular maintenance helps identify small issues before they become major problems, keeping your fleet safer, more reliable, and more profitable.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "fig-1",
                  "type": "image",
                  "props": {
                    "width": "full",
                    "image": {
                      "src": "/img/blog/why-fleets-should-get-regular-trailer-service/1.jpg",
                      "width": 1280,
                      "height": 853,
                      "alt": "International day cab and trailer parked in the Sun State trailer yard"
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-why-matters",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Why Regular Trailer Service Matters",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "why-matters"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-why-matters-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Every mile puts stress on your trailer's major components. Brakes wear down, suspension parts loosen, tires lose tread, bearings experience friction, and electrical systems are exposed to moisture and road debris. Routine trailer service allows technicians to inspect these systems before a minor concern turns into a costly breakdown.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-why-matters-2",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
