                },
                {
                  "id": "p-included-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Professional trailer maintenance involves much more than changing worn parts. Every service appointment is an opportunity to evaluate the overall health of the trailer. A comprehensive inspection typically includes:",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h3-included-2",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Brake System Inspection",
                    "headingLevel": 3,
                    "align": "left"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-included-3",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Trailer brakes are one of the most important safety systems on the vehicle. Technicians inspect brake shoes, drums, chambers, air lines, slack adjusters, and overall brake performance to ensure everything is operating properly.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h3-included-4",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Suspension Components",
                    "headingLevel": 3,
                    "align": "left"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-included-5",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Suspension systems absorb constant stress from heavy loads and rough roads. Worn bushings, damaged springs, or failing suspension components can lead to uneven tire wear and reduced stability.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h3-included-6",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Tires and Wheels",
                    "headingLevel": 3,
                    "align": "left"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-included-7",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Proper tire pressure and healthy tread help maximize fuel efficiency while reducing the chance of roadside blowouts. During trailer service, technicians inspect:",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "checks-included-8",
